      "name": "p256-signature-r-above-the-group-order",
      "sections": [
        "7.1",
        "14.3",
        "11.2 P11"
      ],
      "note": "`r` is an x-coordinate already reduced modulo `n`, so a conforming signer can never emit one at or above the group order; the rejection is on the ENCODING and precedes any curve arithmetic. §16.3 F17 requires the above-the-order case for `r` as well as for `s`, because a validator that range-checked only `s` would pass every other signature case in this family.",
